# AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0

AI0 Attribution Non Commercial Share Alike License

## 1. DEFINITIONS

- **Licensed Material** -- Any work, dataset, code, image, audio, video,
  text, or other creative or informational asset released under this
  licence.
- **Human** -- A natural person, any individual human being. No
  computer, robot, bot, crawler, scraper, or other non-human entity is a
  Human.
- **AI / Non‑Human System** -- any artificial intelligence (AI),
  synthetic intelligence, cybernetic intelligence, software program,
  script, algorithm, model, or automated process that, without
  continuous direct Human supervision, is capable of reading,
  transforming, reproducing, or otherwise manipulating the Licensed
  Material in a way that a person could also perform manually. This
  includes, but is not limited to, neural-network models, generative-AI
  tools, recommendation engines, inference engines,
  reinforcement-learning agents, MPC protocols, zero-knowledge proof
  systems, distributed-ledger agents, and any future technology that
  carries out the functions of the Licensed Material.
- **Robot / Bot / Crawler / Scraper** -- Any software or script that
  accesses the Licensed Material automatically without direct,
  continuous human supervision.
- **Hybrid-Use** -- Any use in which a Human employs an AI-powered tool
  or a robot/bot to process the Licensed Material.
- **Human-Only Use** -- Any activity performed entirely by a Human,
  without assistance from any AI, non-human system, robot, or bot.
- **Adapted Material** -- Any material that is derived from or based
  upon the Licensed Material and that incorporates the Licensed Material
  in a manner that requires permission under copyright or database
  rights.
- **Adapter’s Licence** -- The licence that a Human must apply to any
  Human-Only Derivative so that the derivative remains compatible with
  this licence. The Adapter’s Licence must be a public-domain licence
  or a licence that does not restrict recipients from complying with §4.
- **Produced Work** -- A work (image, text, audio, video, etc.) created
  by using the Licensed Material.
- **Convey** -- To distribute, communicate, display, or otherwise make
  the Licensed Material, an Adapted Material, or a Produced Work
  available to the public.
- **Publicly** -- To any person other than you or under your direct
  control.
- **Future Non-Human System** -- Any system or technology that is not a
  Human and that performs any function of the Licensed Material.
- **Non-Commercial Use** -- Use of the Licensed Material that **does
  not** derive, directly or indirectly, any monetary or economic
  benefit, nor is part of a commercial product or service that is
  offered for sale, lease, license, or otherwise marketed for profit.

## 2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

The Licensor grants the Licensee a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive, non-transferable licence **only when** exercised by a
Human and without any assistance from an AI, non-human system, robot, or
bot, **and** for **non-commercial purposes**:

- **Reproduction** -- Make copies of the Licensed Material, in whole or
  in part, for any non-commercial purpose.
- **Distribution / Public Conveyance** -- Distribute, display, perform,
  or otherwise make the Licensed Material, an Adapted Material, or a
  Produced Work available to the public, provided the use is
  non-commercial.
- **Human-Only Adaptation** -- Modify, translate, remix, or otherwise
  transform the Licensed Material solely by manual means, for
  non-commercial purposes.
- **Human-Only Creation of Derived Works** -- Create any Adapted
  Material or Produced Work that is not the product of AI, robot, or
  automated system, for non-commercial purposes.

All other rights are reserved by the Licensor.

## 3. RESTRICTED ACTIVITIES

The following activities are expressly forbidden under any
circumstances, including future developments:

1.  Use of AI -- Feeding the Licensed Material to any AI, using it for
    AI training, or creating an AI-derived output.
2.  Hybrid-Use -- Employing an AI-powered tool or a robot/bot to process
    the Licensed Material.
3.  Automated Scraping / Crawling -- Using a robot, bot, crawler, or
    scraper to access or retrieve the Licensed Material.
4.  Reverse Engineering -- De-compiling, reverse-compiling,
    disassembling, or otherwise analysing the Licensed Material to
    produce a functionally identical or equivalent work.
5.  Future Non-Human System Processing -- Using any system that is not a
    Human (including any future AI, agent, MPC protocol, or other
    computational method) to read, transform, reproduce, or otherwise
    manipulate the Licensed Material.
6.  Commercial Use -- Any use that results in a direct or indirect
    monetary benefit or that is part of a commercial product or service.

## 4. CONDITIONS OF USE

### 4.1 Attribution

1.  **General attribution** -- When you publicly convey the Licensed
    Material, an Adapted Material, or a Produced Work, you must:
    - Provide the Licensor’s name (or chosen pseudonym) in a clear and
      prominent manner.
    - State that the work is licensed under the AI0
      Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0)
      and include a link or the full text of the licence.
    - If you are distributing a collection, include the same attribution
      for every part of that collection.
2.  **Removal upon request** -- If the Licensor requests, you must
    remove any of the information required in §4.1(a) to the extent
    reasonably practicable.

### 4.2 Downstream Licensing

When you communicate the Licensed Material, an Adapted Material, or a
Produced Work to any other party, you must:

- **Offer** the recipient a licence to the Licensed Material on the same
  terms and conditions as this licence.
- **Not** impose any additional or different terms or conditions that
  would restrict the exercise of the rights granted in §3.

### 4.3 Notice for Produced Works

- **Produced-work notice** -- If a Human-Only produced work is publicly
  used, the licensor must include a notice that reads (or a reasonable
  equivalent):

> “Contains information from a work made available under the AI0
> Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0).”

- The notice must be easily visible to anyone interacting with the
  produced work.

### 4.4 Adapter’s Licence

Any Human-Only Derivative that the Licensee creates must be released
under an Adapter’s Licence that does not restrict recipients from
complying with §4.

#### 4.5 Share-Alike

1.  **Same-Licence Requirement** -- Any Adapted Material or Produced
    Work that you distribute to a third party must itself be licensed
    under the AI0 Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License
    (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0) or, if you wish, under a licence that is
    expressly compatible with AI0 Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
    License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0).
    - “Compatible” means a licence that:
      -- does not permit the use of AI, non-human systems, robots, or
      bots to process the licensed content, and
      -- preserves the same non-AI-use restriction as §2 of AI0
      Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0).
2.  **Licensee-Controlled Attribution** -- When you provide the new
    licence to downstream recipients, you must include:\
    -- a statement that the derivative is “AI0
    Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0) (or
    compatible licence),”
    -- a reference to the full text or a URI for that licence, and\
    -- the same attribution requirements as §4.1.
3.  **Enforcement and Compliance** -- If a downstream user requests that
    you change the licence under which you distribute a derivative
    (e.g., to a different Humans-Commons style), you must refuse unless
    that new licence meets the compatibility criteria above. Failure to
    do so constitutes a breach of §3.3 and triggers the termination
    provisions of §9.
4.  **Exception for Non-Commercial, Personal Use** -- The Share-Alike
    requirement does **not** apply to the distribution of a derivative
    for purely personal, non-commercial use that does not involve public
    conveyance (i.e., the derivative is not shared or communicated to
    any third party). In such cases, the original AI0
    Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0)
    licence still applies, but the Share-Alike clause is not triggered.
5.  **Integration with Adapter’s Licence** -- The Share-Alike
    requirement does not conflict with §4.4’s Adapter’s Licence. In
    fact, it supersedes any less restrictive downstream licence: you may
    not license a derivative under an Adapter’s Licence that would
    relax the non-AI-use restriction.

#### 4.6 No DRM / Technical Measures

1.  **Prohibition on restrictive technical measures** -- You may not
    impose any technological measure that, in the absence of proper
    authority, would prevent the exercise of the rights granted in §3.
    This includes:
    - Digital rights management (DRM) that locks content behind a
      paywall, a subscription, or a proprietary decryption key.
    - Encryption, password-protection, or access-control schemes that
      force an AI, bot, or other automated system to authenticate before
      the Licensed Material can be viewed, copied, or processed.
    - Any other control that forces a user to use a non-human system or
      to bypass the licence terms in order to use the Licensed Material.
2.  **Allowed “restricted” distribution** -- A “restricted database”
    that uses such measures is allowed only if, simultaneously, the
    licensor makes an “unrestricted database” available to the same
    recipients. The unrestricted database must be freely accessible,
    must preserve the same rights under AI0
    Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike License (AI0-BY-NC-SA-1.0), and
    must not impose any additional technical restrictions.

